    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1236">

                <pb facs="1000" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4251.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad Juárez to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Juárez</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s June 19, 2 p.m. No Federal troops approaching Juárez. Governor of
                    Texas probably misinformed. Mexican consul <pb facs="1001" n="885"
                        xml:id="pg885"/> El Paso assures me no movement contemplated at present for
                    retaking Juárez. Personal observations confirm this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
